WikiReader Gen2 @VERSION@
==========================
New software for the Openmoko WikiReader that reads current Wikipedia
(Kiwix ZIM) files.

You need
--------
* An Openmoko WikiReader
* A microSD card formatted FAT32 (8 GB or larger recommended). Cards over
  32 GB are usually sold as exFAT and must be reformatted to FAT32 first.
* A separate card: this is the software for the card, nothing inside the
  WikiReader is changed. Your original card keeps working.

Install
-------
1. Format the card as FAT32 (one partition, Master Boot Record).
   Windows: cards up to 32 GB can be formatted in Explorer (FAT32).
   Linux:   sudo mkfs.vfat -F 32 /dev/sdX1
   macOS:   Disk Utility, "MS-DOS (FAT)", Master Boot Record.
2. Copy all the files and folders to the top (root) of the card, keeping
   the folders as they are (extract them first if you downloaded a zip).
   The card should then hold kernel.elf, init.app, WIKIFONT.BIN,
   ZWSTATE.DAT and one folder per wiki (e.g. ENPEDIA).
3. Eject the card safely, put it in the WikiReader and switch on.
4. The first start of each wiki shows "Preparing" and its name for a few
   seconds. This only happens once.

Updating an existing card
-------------------------
Copy only init.app (and kernel.elf and WIKIFONT.BIN if they changed) over
the old ones. Keep ZWSTATE.DAT and the .HIS and .EXT files in the wiki
folders: they hold your place and history. ZWSTATE.DAT is only for a new
card.

Using it
--------
SEARCH          search screen, as you left it (press again to clear)
HISTORY         short press: Back.  Hold: list of recent articles
RANDOM          random article
Type            results update as you type, tap one to open it
                (drag the results to put the keyboard away, tap the
                search bar to bring it back; 123 for digits)
Drag            scroll (flick to scroll faster)
Tap a link      open it (links have a dotted underline)
Tap the page    toolbar: Back, List (sections), Top, Prev, Next
Bottom left     tap the corner of an article to go Back
Wiki name       tap it on the empty search screen to switch wiki
Footnotes, Citations
                switches on the empty search screen (tap to turn on or
                off; used from the next article). On: [a] and [1] markers
                in the text and the Notes and References lists at the
                end. Tap a marker to jump to its note, ^ to jump back
Power           saves your place and switches off (also after 2 minutes)

Adding other wikis
------------------
Any Kiwix ZIM can be added (Wikipedia, Wiktionary, Wikivoyage...), up to
32 wikis per card. Always prepare it on a PC with zimprep (in the source
package) and copy the folder it makes to the card. Do not copy .zim files
to the card directly. Full instructions are in the README.md inside the
source package.

Problems
--------
* The WikiReader shows its contrast menu, as if there were no card: some
  microSD cards are not recognised by the WikiReader's built-in loader.
  Try a different make of card.
* "No card": the card is not FAT32, or the card type is not supported.
  Try another card. Known to work: SanDisk Extreme PRO 64 GB (A2),
  SanDisk Ultra PLUS 200 GB (U1).
  Not recognised: Gigastone 128 GB (A1).
* "No wiki found": the wiki folder is missing or nested in another folder.
  It must be at the top of the card, e.g. MATHS/MATHS.IDX.

Feedback
--------
This is a test release and feedback is very welcome: @FEEDBACK@
Please say which wiki and article, what you did, and what happened.
A photo of the screen helps a lot. The version is shown at the bottom
of the search screen.

